    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "When a rule-breaking casting decision saw Lupita Nyong'o chosen for Helen of Troy and Clytemnestra, it ignited fierce digital backlash. Self-appointed guardians of tradition leveled accusations of cultural erasure, framing the move as an attack on European heritage. But truth-tellers against gatekeeping countered, arguing the Western canon is shared civilizational property, turning this public debate into a clear battle line between orthodoxy and those claiming the story.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Outlaw",
