    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The announcement of a disruptive casting choice in Christopher Nolan's Homer adaptation sparked a cultural conflict. Establishment voices accused the film project of historical revisionism, a charge met by rebels who reframed the canon as collective property. This ideological conflict has exposed the entrenched order's resistance, proving that a simple casting decision can become a flashpoint over who owns classical stories in mass-market film.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Outlaw",
